Choosing the right chart:
    1. Scatterplot:
        Shows relationships between two variables
    2. Boxplot:
        Compare distribution across categories
        eg: mean radius across malignant vs benign groups
    3. Heatmap:
        Summarize many relationships at once
        eg: correlation matrix of all tumor features

Avoid misleading visuals:
    1. Proper scaling:
        Don't truncate axes unless you explicitly want to highligh small differences
    2. Honest color maps
        Avoid rainbow colormaps
        Prefer viridis, coolwarm
    3. Clear labelling
        Label units, categories, and axes

Building Narrative Dashboards
    1. Combine multiple plots
        use subplots or matplotlib.gridspec to arrange scatterplots, boxplots, and heatmaps together
    2. Guide the user's eye
        Place the most important plot in the top-left or center
        Use consistent color scheme (malignant -> red, Benign -> blue)
    3. Tell a story
        Heatmap shows collinearity among tumor features 
        Scatterplot highlights separation between malignant and benign
        Boxplot compares distribution of a key feature 

        